ge, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adverbs of Manner", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "If we want to describe how something is done, we can use adverbs of manner.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Adverbs of manner are usually found in different types of tenses.  <br /> <br />  Present continuous.  <br />  <li><span class=\"italic\">The world of food is seriously dealing with some issues of sexism.</span> </li> <br />   Present perfect.  <br />  <li><span class=\"italic\">I have consistently been an advocate of home cooked meals.</span></li> <br />  Simple present.  <br /> <li><span class=\"italic\">Celebrity chefs you regularly see on television tend to be male.</span></li> <br />  After infinitives.  <br /> <li><span class=\"italic\">You need to plan carefully.</span></li> <br /> It is also possible to find more than one adverb in a sentences, and sometimes after more.  <br /> <li><span class=\"italic\">Studies have repeatedly demonstrated that women cook more frequently than men, even in the modern family.</span></li>  <br />   Don't forget that <span class=\"italic\">fast, hard, well</span> and <span class=\"italic\">straight</span> are both adjectives and adverbs and they do not change when they become adverbs. Remember that you can form an adverb from an adjective by adding <span class =\"strong\">-ly</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adverb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"consistent</br> serious</br>\\t\\t endless</br> careful\\t</br>\\t regular\\t\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"consistently</br> seriously </br>endlessly</br> carefully</br> regularly\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Superlatives and Comparatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When using superlatives, it is important to know if an adjective is long or short. Adjectives are long when they have more than one syllable in pronunciation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Examples</span>:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><ul>  \t<li>Cooking is more common in modern families. </li> \t<li>Men and women are cooking more exotic dishes. </li> \t<li>Usually men cook the most delicious dishes at home.</li>  </ul>   \t</span>\t\t", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you have a one-syllable adjective in pronunciation,  or you have a two-syllable adjective in pronunciation whose final letter is<span class = \"strong\"> -y</span>, then you have a short adjective.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Examples</span>:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><ul> <li>Families are trying to prepare healthier dishes at home. </li> \t<li>Learning to cook is a lot easier these days. </li> \t<li>Celebrity chefs prepare the fanciest plates.</li> </ul>   \t\t\t</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use comparatives with adverbs of manner to make more emphasis in the way the action is done.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Examples</span>:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><ul>  \t<li>Women cook more frequently than men. </li> \t<li>When you want to buy local products, you need to plan more carefully.</li> </ul>   \t\t\t</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": 