ave consistently been an advocate of home cooked meals -- especially if they are prepared by somebody else. But who is that somebody else? Studies have repeatedly demonstrated that women cook more frequently than men, even in the modern family.  42% of men spend time in the kitchen, compared to 84% of women.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": ""}, {"text": "Have you ever seen a cookbook called something like <span class=\"italic\">Great Recipes for Busy Moms</span>? The reality is that cooking takes time. When you want to buy local products, you need to plan carefully. If you have vegetarians in the family, you need to do research.", "id": 2, "time": "20000", "image": ""}, {"text": "The world of food is seriously dealing with some issues of sexism. Celebrity chefs you regularly see on television tend to be male. They prepare exotic dishes with fancy sauces. It looks great on television, but women have less time to prepare that way at home.  Men are better at selling supplements and vitamins, but women are the ones usually putting food on the table at home, three meals a day.", "id": 3, "time": "33200", "image": ""}], "video_src": "engenn6le13ob10re2vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "_data": [], "type": "video", "template_override": 1}]}]}